				864,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose FileSystem module and add native readdir handler\n\nReplace the FileSystem glob import with explicit submodule paths for all Managed (trait-based) and Native (tokio::fs) file operations. Add new FileReaddirNative handler under FileSystem/Native/ implementing the file:readdir wire method using tokio::fs.\n\nThis continues the module decomposition pattern from recent commits, replacing the monolithic FileSystem.rs with granular domain-specific handlers. The explicit paths follow CLAUDE.md requirements, making dependency relationships clear at every call site.\n\nNo functional changes - this is a pure refactoring for code organization and maintainability.",
			"SHA": "70c31747d3943f857b4c7bc9644f8fd469b0dd76"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T20:54:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				864,
				42
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Simplify binary names and split monolithic IPC handlers\n\nRename the Cargo binary and lib from the verbose development profile name to simply 'Mountain', matching the tauri.conf.json productName simplification. Concurrently, decompose the monolithic NativeHost.rs into 10 domain-specific handler files under WindServiceHandlers/NativeHost/ (FindFreePort, GetColorScheme, IsFullscreen, IsMaximized, OpenExternal, OSProperties, OSStatistics, PickFolder, ShowItemInFolder, ShowOpenDialog).\n\nAlso introduce a new FileSystem module split into Managed (trait-based) and Native (tokio::fs) tiers, each with their own atom handlers. Update mod.rs to replace the NativeHost glob import with explicit submodule paths, consistent with the reverse-hierarchical path pattern enforced in recent commits.",
			"SHA": "fb4a24fd951420127e59e433b3a268432fbcf6da"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T19:11:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				829,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Complete explicit module path migration in state and IPC\n\nContinue the refactoring from commit 10feb14ec to eliminate implicit module namespace reliance by fully qualifying internal paths:\n\n- Add explicit `TextProcessing` segment in DocumentStateDTO import for `AnalyzeTextLinesAndEOL`\n- Prefix ConfigurationState, UIState, and WorkspaceState type paths with their module name (e.g., `UIState::UIState::State`)\n- Update WorkspaceDelta function signatures with full `WorkspaceState::WorkspaceState::State` paths\n- Migrate AppLifecycle call site from `WindServiceHandlers::set_static_application_root` to `WindServiceHandlers::Utilities::set_static_application_root`\n\nThis ensures all internal references use the reverse-hierarchical path pattern that makes dependency relationships explicit in every call site, consistent with the CLAUDE.md module path requirements.",
			"SHA": "e3135b994ecc9c8cbedf24de93c125e810437122"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T19:05:06Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				829,
				14
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Enforce explicit module paths, eliminate pub use re-exports\n\nPer CLAUDE.md requirements, replace `pub use` glob re-exports with local `use` statements throughout Mountain's IPC and state modules. This enforces that callers spell full qualified paths like `WindServiceHandlers::Utilities::get_static_application_root()` rather than relying on flattened namespace imports.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove `pub use *` from WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs, UI/mod.rs, and ApplicationState modules\n- Convert to local `use X::*` scoped to the dispatcher file only\n- Update call sites in Scheme.rs, AppLifecycle.rs, and Search.rs to use explicit paths\n- Reorganize module declaration order in FeatureState and Internal modules\n\nThe reverse-hierarchical path is load-bearing - it tells the reader which file owns the handler. This change prevents accidental namespace pollution and makes dependency relationships explicit in every call site.\n\nAlso updates tauri.conf.json to include externalBin for node binary.",
			"SHA": "10feb14ec590c0361e9a0038e0833bf752bf447e"
		}
	],
